        bounds leave free: gamma = gamma-tilde/(1 + c)
    E[(alpha2 U)^3], the confounder's        0.819511
    E[V2^3]                                  0.021739  (hme takes it 0)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Over-identification at order four: nine moments, eight parameters
    profiled GMM, method(pgmm): orders 2 and 3 fitted exactly
        gamma                                0.445316
        J, 1 df                                  0.1426   P>chi2 0.7057
        the joint GMM, and the region where its J stays within
        3.84 of its minimum: method(gmm) or method(all)
    B kurt_U - A kurt_V2                         0.2268   z   1.15
    The J tests alpha1 = gamma alpha2.  The Jacobian of the
    model with alpha1 FREE has determinant -(gamma - tau)^5
    times the factor above, so the restriction is testable
    everywhere except where that factor vanishes -- and a
    normal V2 sits exactly there, since it makes both B and
    kurt_V2 zero.
    The J does not reject AND the factor is not distinguishable
    from zero, so this non-rejection carries no information
    about scale consistency: the design is near the surface
    where the restriction cannot be tested at all.
    The factor's magnitude is NOT a calibrated measure of power;
    only its vanishing, under the null, is meaningful.
------------------------------------------------------------------------
s.e.: delta method on the stacked moments; the estimation of the
coefficients on X is accounted for.  The QME's own standard error is
proportional to 1/sqrt(D): it explodes as the discriminant nears zero.

