. * ======================================================================
. * Section 4.4 -- an estimate from elsewhere: Card's IV against the interval
. * ======================================================================
. quietly freeiv lwage exper expersq black south smsa (educ)

. freeivtest, gamma(0.132) segamma(0.049)

freeiv agreement tests                             Number of obs =      3010
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Endogeneity itself: theta = 0, with no estimate of gamma
    E[r eps2^2] = m12 - gt m03                   0.039853
    E[r^2 eps2] = m21 - 2gt m12 + gt^2 m03       0.002892
    Wald, chi2(2)                                  1.4271   P>chi2 0.4899
    r is the OLS residual of xi on eps2.  Under theta = 0 it is
    independent of eps2, not merely uncorrelated, so both cross
    moments vanish.  This never estimates gamma, so it keeps its
    power where the qme loses its own (small D).
    Read it with z(m03) from -freeivmenu-: detecting theta > 0 needs
    m03 != 0 from either U or V2, while ESTIMATING gamma needs
    A = alpha2^3 E[U^3] != 0, a skewed confounder.  The two signals
    are different, so detection can succeed where estimation fails.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pairwise agreement between the closed forms (reference: qme)
  pair            difference        s.e.         z    P>|z|   tests
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  qme - ols        -0.001863    0.254307     -0.01   0.9942   theta = 0
  qme - hme                .           .         .        .   B = 0
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
theta = 0: no confounding.  B = 0: V2 symmetric, as the hme assumes.
A large |z| says the two routes disagree by more than sampling
noise, so the assumption that separates them is rejected.  A small
|z| is mutual corroboration: two routes with different assumptions
agree.  None of these tests scale consistency -- they presuppose it.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Outside estimate   0.132000 against the identified set
    bounds [0.037004, 0.074009]   s.e. 0.001819 and 0.003638
    distance to the upper bound                  0.057991
    z                                              1.1802   P>|z| 0.2379
    => outside the set: under scale consistency no value of
    gamma can produce this estimate without a negative
    variance.  Run -freeivdiag, gamma(.132)- to see which.
    (the two standard errors are added as if independent,
    which they are not -- they come from the same sample)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

. 
