Reading: the pair must be relevant (t >= 10) and the two third-order
cross-moments must share a sign, or Theorem 1 has nothing to work
with; a guard that fires here will fire in freeiv.  The implied
skewness sets the precision: near 0.5 the causal coefficient is
recovered but the free direct effect a1 is not; above 1.5 all
parameters are precise and scale consistency becomes testable.
The one-factor check reads only when the third order is strong;
a profile whose minimum is interior does not bound anything.

